  "articleBody": "So, you’re knee-deep in a remodel and suddenly, framing questions pop up. It’s super common to wonder if a wall is load-bearing or what changes are needed for a new opening. These are big questions because they directly affect your home's stability and how other systems like plumbing or electrical will run. Sometimes, folks get tripped up by not confirming the final layout before starting demolition or by ordering materials too late. This can really throw a wrench in the timeline, causing rework and delays that nobody wants! You also need to coordinate with other trades and inspections. For instance, if you're making structural modifications or adding new openings, a licensed contractor and maybe even a structural engineer become important players. They ensure the work is safe, stable, and passes inspection, which ultimately keeps your project moving smoothly. If you're feeling overwhelmed, don't hesitate to reach out. We can help you get things back on track.",
